SUMMARY:Women's Freedom Center's Femmes & Thems Collage Club
LOCATION:Meeting Room A – Community Meeting Room\, 224 Main Street\, Bra
 ttleboro\, VT\, 05301\, United States
URL:https://brookslibraryvt.org/event/womens-freedom-centers-femmes-thems-
 collage-club/2026-10-02/
CATEGORIES:kids\,Brooks Memorial Library
DESCRIPTION:The Women’s Freedom Center is hosting a Femmes and Thems
  Collage Club for survivors of Intimate Partner Violence\, Sexual Violen
 ce and their Allies on the first Friday of every month from 1:30PM- 3PM at
  Brooks Memorial Library in the Community Room on the third floor. We have
  supplies galore and good conversation. Bring your own collage materials\,
  or just yourself.\nSource: Brooks Memorial Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:80efa821b23358ae@kidcal
DTSTAMP:20260920T143252Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261004T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261004T190000
SUMMARY:Sci-Fi Film Series: BLADE RUNNER
LOCATION:The Latchis Theatre\, 50 Main Street\, Brattleboro\, Vermont\, 05
 301\, United States
URL:https://brookslibraryvt.org/event/sci-fi-film-series-blade-runner/
CATEGORIES:kids\,Brooks Memorial Library
DESCRIPTION:The Sci-Fi Film Series is your chance to see great and classic
  Sci-Fi films on the big screen! Join us at the Latchis Theater to watch t
 his month’s film: the “Final Cut” of 1982’s cyberpunk classic\, Bl
 ade Runner! \nLos Angeles\, California\, 2019. With towering skyscrapers l
 ooming over the dystopian mega-city\, grizzled replicant hunter Rick Decka
 rd (Harrison Ford) is called out of retirement when rogue Nexus-6 replican
 ts steal a spaceship and enter Earth. The order is crystal-clear: Deckard 
 must seek out the illegal replicants and destroy them before they locate t
 heir creator. However\, as Deckard tries to fix the mistakes of those who 
 want to play God\, unprecedented\, conflicting emotions cloud his judgemen
 t. Can uncertainty and empathy overshadow a Blade Runner’s sense of duty
 ? \nAttendees are invited to stay afterward for a discussion about the fil
 m. Admission by donation. \nPresented by Brooks Memorial Library and the L
 atchis Theater. Sponsored by the Friends of Brooks Memorial Library.\nSour
 ce: Brooks Memorial Library
END:VEVENT
